 "text": "Passage graves are ancient tomb mounds with a stone passage. They mark an early way of ritual burial among the megalithic people. Most hold a small inner chamber, where a few mourners could gather. One mound at Fourknocks was large enough for many. Old people later read these tombs as fairy homes, and feared them.",
